ctrvcr.group.screen=Screen
ctrvcr.group.tape=Tape
ctrvcr.group.colour=Colour
ctrvcr.desc.distortion=How much the picture bulges like the glass of a tube. 0 keeps it flat.
ctrvcr.desc.scanlines=Dark and bright rows across the picture. Higher makes them stronger.
ctrvcr.desc.scanline_size=Pixels per scanline. 0 keeps about 540 lines at any resolution.
ctrvcr.desc.dark_edges=Darkens the left and right edges like the tube's walls.
ctrvcr.desc.blur=Red and blue drift apart and blur like a worn tape. 0 keeps the picture sharp.
ctrvcr.desc.bloom=Soft glow round bright parts, jittered like the tape. 0 turns it off.
ctrvcr.desc.grain=Noise over the picture. Higher is grainier.
ctrvcr.desc.static=White specks of static. Higher shows more.
ctrvcr.desc.tear=A band that rolls up the picture now and then. 0 turns it off.
ctrvcr.desc.tint_green=The tape's green cast. 1 is neutral.
ctrvcr.desc.saturation=Strength of colour. 1 leaves it as it is.
ctrvcr.desc.black_white=Fades the picture to black and white.
ctrvcr.desc.color_levels=Fewer colours with dither, like a cheap capture. 0 keeps every colour.
ctrvcr.desc.warm_light=Torches and the light in your hand turn warmer, as under an old tube.
ctrvcr.preset.default=CTR VCR
ctrvcr.preset.default.desc=The pack's own look, as CTR VCR ships it.
ctrvcr.preset.clean=Clean CRT
ctrvcr.preset.clean.desc=A good TV: curve and scanlines, little tape.
ctrvcr.preset.worn=Worn Tape
ctrvcr.preset.worn.desc=A tape played a hundred times: smear, static, tears.
ctrvcr.preset.mono=Monochrome
ctrvcr.preset.mono.desc=A black and white set.
